        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Yes, this behavior is intentional for two reasons:\r\n- It is indeed proved useful for reference during quick edit of another window. Just used this today.\r\n- Technically, any window always has \"cursor\" tracked, even if it is not active. So there is still cursor when you leave window.\r\n\r\nSorry, I don't see this changed in the near future.",
